rnels\\mean.cl: #pragma OPENCL EXTENSION cl_khr_fp16 : enable\r #pragma OPENCL EXTENSION cl_khr_subgroups : enable\r \r // Most devices have max workgroup size of 1024, so this is enough for subgroup\r // sizes of 16, 32, 64 and 128. Increase this value for smaller subgroups sizes\r #define MAX_SUBGROUPS 64\r kernel void kernel_mean_f32(\r     global char *  src0,\r     ulong           offset0,\r     global char *  dst,\r ","id":"file_map:ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-opencl\\kernels\\mean.cl","metadata":{"extension":"cl","geometry_map":[-0.049978140741586685,0.03863513097167015,0.02964344434440136,0.03998612239956856,0.03193126618862152,0.034330323338508606,0.036901481449604034,-0.026959367096424103,-0.01737160235643387,0.018261363729834557],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-opencl\\kernels\\mean.cl","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.0,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":3534},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"file_map","content":"ROCmFPX\\examples\\model-conversion\\scripts\\utils\\hf-upload-gguf-model.py: #!/usr/bin/env python3\r \r from huggingface_hub import HfApi\r import argparse\r import os\r \r def upload_gguf_file(local_file_path, repo_id, filename_in_repo=None):\r     \"\"\"\r     Upload a GGUF file to a Hugging Face model repository\r \r     Args:\r         local_file_path: Path to your local GGUF file\r         repo_id: Your repository ID (e.g., \"username/model-name\")\r         filename_in_repo: Optional","id":"file_map:ROCmFPX\\examples\\model-conversion\\scripts\\utils\\hf-upload-gguf-model.py","metadata":{"extension":"py","geometry_map":[-0.036143213510513306,0.03580157086253166,0.03137609362602234,0.02869756519794464,0.031047044321894646,0.045099157840013504,0.030723320320248604,-0.02834746055305004,-0.013890278525650501,0.0010236621601507068],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\examples\\model-conversion\\scripts\\utils\\hf-upload-gguf-model.py","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.30000001192092896,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":2030},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"fix_lessons","content":"ROCmFPX\\docs\\BUILD-AMD-ARCHITECTURES.md: # Building ROCmFP4 for AMD GPUs\r \r ROCmFP4 runs on **CPU**, **Vulkan**, and **ROCm/HIP**. Most users want the HIP\r backend for best performance. To build HIP support, you must compile for your\r GPU's `gfx` target.\r \r Vulkan does not need a `gfx` target at compile time and works across RDNA2+ AMD\r GPUs, but HIP performance tuning in this tree is strongest on Strix Halo.\r \r ---\r \r ## Choose Your Build Path\r \r | Your GPU | Example cards | Easiest build command | Build output folder |\r |---|---|---|---|\r | **Strix Halo / RDNA3.5** | Ryzen AI MAX+ 395, Framework Desktop | `scripts/build-strix-rocmfp4-mtp.sh` | `build-strix-rocmfp4/` |\r | **RDNA2** | RX 6700 XT, RX 6800 | `scripts/build-rdna2.sh` | `build-rdna2/` |\r | **RDNA3** | RX 7600, RX 7900 XTX, RX 7800 XT | `scripts/build-rdna3.sh` | `build-rdna3/` |\r | **RDNA4** | RX 9070 XT | `scripts/build-rdna4.sh` | `build-rdna4/` |\r | **Vega 20 / gfx906 experimental** | Radeon Instinct MI50 / MI60 | `scripts/build-gfx906.sh` | `build-gfx906/` |\r | **Windows RDNA2** | RX 6000 series on Windows | `build-hip.bat` | `build-hip/` |\r | **Vulkan only** | Any AMD GPU with Vulkan drivers | see [Vulkan-only build](#vulkan-only-no-hip-arch-needed) | `b","id":"fix_lessons:ROCmFPX\\docs\\BUILD-AMD-ARCHITECTURES.md","metadata":{"extension":"md","geometry_map":[-0.03192581236362457,0.040425874292850494,0.03579125180840492,0.02759038284420967,0.03250860795378685,0.039525002241134644,0.02990611456334591,-0.025026235729455948,-0.024682430550456047,0.00640843715518713],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\docs\\BUILD-AMD-ARCHITECTURES.md","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.0,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":10671},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"fix_lessons","content":"ROCmFPX\\docs\\development\\debugging-tests.md: # Debugging Tests Tips\r \r ## How to run & execute or debug a specific test without anything else to keep the feedback loop short?\r \r There is a script called debug-test.sh in the scripts folder whose parameter takes a REGEX and an optional test number.\r \r For example, running the following command will output an interactive list from which you can select a test. It takes this form:\r \r `debug-test.sh [OPTION]... <test_regex> <test_number>`\r \r It will then build & run in the debugger for you.\r \r To just execute a test and get back a PASS or FAIL message run:\r \r ```bash\r ./scripts/debug-test.sh test-tokenizer\r ```\r \r To test in GDB use the `-g` flag to enable gdb test mode.\r \r ```bash\r ./scripts/debug-test.sh -g test-tokenizer\r \r # Once in the debugger, i.e. at the chevrons prompt, setting a breakpoint could be as follows:\r >>> b main\r ```\r \r To speed up the testing loop, if you know your test number you can just run it similar to below:\r \r ```bash\r ./scripts/debug-test.sh test 23\r ```\r \r For further reference use `debug-test.sh -h` to print help.\r \r &nbsp;\r \r ### How does the script work?\r If you want to be able to use the concepts contained in the script separately, the important on","id":"fix_lessons:ROCmFPX\\docs\\development\\debugging-tests.md","metadata":{"extension":"md","geometry_map":[-0.03275779262185097,0.04345269128680229,0.03991801664233208,0.026658061891794205,0.029921365901827812,0.041736651211977005,0.027752259746193886,-0.020500047132372856,-0.024482442066073418,0.0037911890540271997],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\docs\\development\\debugging-tests.md","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.30000001192092896,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":3283},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"file_map","content":"ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-vulkan\\vulkan-shaders\\dequant_q6_k.comp: #version 450\r \r #include \"dequant_head.glsl\"\r \r layout(local_size_x = 64, local_size_y = 1, local_size_z = 1) in;\r \r layout (binding = 0) readonly buffer A {A_TYPE data_a[];};\r layout (binding = 1) writeonly buffer D {D_TYPE data_b[];};\r \r void main() {\r     [[unroll]] for (uint wgy = 0; wgy < 256; wgy++) {\r         const uint i = gl_WorkGroupID.x * 256 + wgy;\r         if (i >= p.nel / QUANT_K) {\r","id":"file_map:ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-vulkan\\vulkan-shaders\\dequant_q6_k.comp","metadata":{"extension":"comp","geometry_map":[-0.04663526266813278,0.034757304936647415,0.023671722039580345,0.040144916623830795,0.030601752921938896,0.0366363525390625,0.03919848054647446,-0.0315709225833416,-0.01641126722097397,0.015159353613853455],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-vulkan\\vulkan-shaders\\dequant_q6_k.comp","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.0,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":1454},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"file_map","content":"ROCmFPX\\examples\\model-conversion\\scripts\\causal\\run-org-model.py: #!/usr/bin/env python3\r \r import argparse\r import os\r import sys\r import importlib\r import torch\r import numpy as np\r \r from transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoModelForImageTextToText, AutoConfig\r \r # Add parent directory to path for imports\r sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), '..'))\r from utils.common import debug_hook, save_output_data\r \r def par","id":"file_map:ROCmFPX\\examples\\model-conversion\\scripts\\causal\\run-org-model.py","metadata":{"extension":"py","geometry_map":[-0.035415176302194595,0.03833490610122681,0.03147240728139877,0.02804821915924549,0.028254512697458267,0.04532396048307419,0.03049657493829727,-0.03015856444835663,-0.013229451142251492,0.0014821498189121485],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\examples\\model-conversion\\scripts\\causal\\run-org-model.py","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.30000001192092896,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":6658},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"file_map","content":"ROCmFPX\\examples\\llama.android\\lib\\src\\test\\java\\android\\llama\\cpp\\ExampleUnitTest.kt: package android.llama.cpp\r \r import org.junit.Test\r \r import org.junit.Assert.*\r \r /**\r  * Example local unit test, which will execute on the development machine (host).\r  *\r  * See [testing documentation](http://d.android.com/tools/testing).\r  */\r class ExampleUnitTest {\r     @Test\r     fun addition_isCorrect() {\r         assertEquals(4, 2 + 2)\r     }\r }\r ","id":"file_map:ROCmFPX\\examples\\llama.android\\lib\\src\\test\\java\\android\\llama\\cpp\\ExampleUnitTest.kt","metadata":{"extension":"kt","geometry_map":[-0.03733891248703003,0.04153934121131897,0.031809985637664795,0.03530086949467659,0.03524400666356087,0.04854375869035721,0.028061240911483765,-0.02887413464486599,-0.020815229043364525,0.007434078026562929],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\examples\\llama.android\\lib\\src\\test\\java\\android\\llama\\cpp\\ExampleUnitTest.kt","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.0,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":359},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"file_map","content":"ROCmFPX\\common\\base64.hpp: /*\r This is free and unencumbered software released into the public domain.\r \r Anyone is free to copy, modify, publish, use, compile, sell, or\r distribute this software, either in source code form or as a compiled\r binary, for any purpose, commercial or non-commercial, and by any\r means.\r \r In jurisdictions that recognize copyright laws, the author or authors\r of this software dedicate any and all","id":"file_map:ROCmFPX\\common\\base64.hpp","metadata":{"extension":"hpp","geometry_map":[-0.04682235047221184,0.03867550194263458,0.040829628705978394,0.03532539680600166,0.015788158401846886,0.04382969066500664,0.023445870727300644,-0.0074287415482103825,-0.015345554798841476,0.0024117010179907084],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\common\\base64.hpp","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.0,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":13270},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"file_map","content":"ROCmFPX\\examples\\llama.android\\lib\\src\\main\\cpp\\ai_chat.cpp: #include <android/log.h>\r #include <jni.h>\r #include <iomanip>\r #include <cmath>\r #include <string>\r #include <unistd.h>\r #include <sampling.h>\r \r #include \"logging.h\"\r #include \"chat.h\"\r #include \"common.h\"\r #include \"llama.h\"\r \r template<class T>\r static std::string join(const std::vector<T> &values, const std::string &delim) {\r     std::ostringstream str;\r     for (size_t i = 0; i < values.size","id":"file_map:ROCmFPX\\examples\\llama.android\\lib\\src\\main\\cpp\\ai_chat.cpp","metadata":{"extension":"cpp","geometry_map":[-0.03719894215464592,0.04163925722241402,0.0317351296544075,0.03541085124015808,0.03524523973464966,0.048191264271736145,0.028833847492933273,-0.027972454205155373,-0.0206892266869545,0.009047082625329494],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\examples\\llama.android\\lib\\src\\main\\cpp\\ai_chat.cpp","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.30000001192092896,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":20219},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"file_map","content":"ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-sycl\\template-instances\\fattn-vec-instance-q5_1-q4_1.cpp: // This file has been autogenerated by generate_cu_files.py, do not edit manually.\r \r #include \"../fattn-vec.hpp\"\r \r DECL_FATTN_VEC_CASE( 64, GGML_TYPE_Q5_1, GGML_TYPE_Q4_1);\r DECL_FATTN_VEC_CASE(128, GGML_TYPE_Q5_1, GGML_TYPE_Q4_1);\r DECL_FATTN_VEC_CASE(256, GGML_TYPE_Q5_1, GGML_TYPE_Q4_1);\r DECL_FATTN_VEC_CASE(512, GGML_TYPE_Q5_1, GGML_TYPE_Q4_1);\r ","id":"file_map:ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-sycl\\template-instances\\fattn-vec-instance-q5_1-q4_1.cpp","metadata":{"extension":"cpp","geometry_map":[-0.047637250274419785,0.036943648010492325,0.025953365489840508,0.0415777787566185,0.03560774773359299,0.03967843949794769,0.03433315455913544,-0.031335894018411636,-0.017118794843554497,0.015200653113424778],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-sycl\\template-instances\\fattn-vec-instance-q5_1-q4_1.cpp","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.0,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":353},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"fix_lessons","content":"ROCmFPX\\docs\\ROCmFP6-COMPETITIVE-EXPERIMENT.md: # ROCmFP6 Competitive Experiment\r \r Status: experimental. These notes cover the Qwythos 9B Claude Mythos 5 1M MTP BF16 source tested on Strix Halo.\r \r ## Presets\r \r Two opt-in ROCmFP6 presets were added without changing existing file types:\r \r - `Q6_0_ROCMFPX_LEAN`: size/speed-biased FP6 routing with no Q8-heavy boosts.\r - `Q6_0_ROCMFPX_AGENT_LEAN`: agent-biased FP6 routing that spends limited `Q6_K` on token/output and selected sensitive projections instead of using the older Q8-heavy agent route.\r \r Existing `Q6_0_ROCMFPX` and `Q6_0_ROCMFPX_AGENT` GGUFs continue to load with their previous routing and tensor types.\r \r ## Qwythos 9B Size And Speed\r \r Command shape:\r \r ```bash\r MODEL_SRC=/mnt/seconddrive/models/Qwythos-9B-Claude-Mythos-5-1M-GGUF/Qwythos-9B-Claude-Mythos-5-1M-MTP-BF16.gguf \\\r OUT_DIR=/tmp/rocmfp6-qwythos-competitive \\\r PRESETS='Q6_K Q6_0_ROCMFPX_LEAN Q6_0_ROCMFPX_AGENT_LEAN' \\\r BACKENDS='ROCm0 Vulkan0' RUN_QUANTIZE=1 RUN_BENCH=1 \\\r PROMPT_TOKENS=512 GEN_TOKENS=128 REPEAT=2 \\\r scripts/sweep-rocmfp6-competitive.sh\r ```\r \r | preset | file MiB | delta vs Q6_K | ROCm pp512 | ROCm tg128 | Vulkan pp512 | Vulkan tg128 |\r |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r | Q6_K | 7208.73","id":"fix_lessons:ROCmFPX\\docs\\ROCmFP6-COMPETITIVE-EXPERIMENT.md","metadata":{"extension":"md","geometry_map":[-0.02722823992371559,0.037913959473371506,0.038782525807619095,0.03234033286571503,0.03098354861140251,0.041405629366636276,0.027935462072491646,-0.02681184560060501,-0.021831074729561806,0.00585657823830843],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\docs\\ROCmFP6-COMPETITIVE-EXPERIMENT.md","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.30000001192092896,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":5174},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"file_map","content":"ROCmFPX\\examples\\gguf-hash\\deps\\sha256\\sha256.c: /* Crypto/Sha256.c -- SHA-256 Hash\r 2010-06-11 : Igor Pavlov : Public domain\r This code is based on public domain code from Wei Dai's Crypto++ library. */\r \r #include \"rotate-bits/rotate-bits.h\"\r #include \"sha256.h\"\r \r /* define it for speed optimization */\r #define _SHA256_UNROLL\r #define _SHA256_UNROLL2\r \r void\r sha256_init(sha256_t *p)\r {\r   p->state[0] = 0x6a09e667;\r   p->state[1] = 0xbb67ae85","id":"file_map:ROCmFPX\\examples\\gguf-hash\\deps\\sha256\\sha256.c","metadata":{"extension":"c","geometry_map":[-0.034728605300188065,0.043180204927921295,0.023842383176088333,0.03373066708445549,0.02934606745839119,0.04201718792319298,0.037587445229291916,-0.022642064839601517,-0.017012758180499077,0.0021506636403501034],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\examples\\gguf-hash\\deps\\sha256\\sha256.c","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.0,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":5503},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"fix_lessons","content":"ROCmFPX\\docs\\ROCmFP6-DECODE-FOLLOWUP.md: # ROCmFP6 Decode Follow-Up\r \r Date: 2026-06-27\r \r Model:\r \r `/mnt/seconddrive/models/Qwythos-9B-Claude-Mythos-5-1M-GGUF`\r \r Commands used `llama-bench -p 512 -n 128 -ngl 999 -fa on -ctk f16 -ctv f16 -b 2048 -ub 512 -t 16`, with `-r 3` for final-state checks and `-r 5` for probes.\r \r ## Current Comparison\r \r | Quant | Backend | Size | pp512 tok/s | tg128 tok/s |\r |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r | Q6_0_ROCMFPX_AGENT, packed default | ROCm0 | 8.06 GiB | 730.16 | 25.59 |\r | Q6_0_ROCMFPX_AGENT, expanded-device experiment | ROCm0 | 8.06 GiB | 737.98 | 23.76 |\r | Q6_K | ROCm0 | 7.08 GiB | 794.78 | 28.97 |\r | Q6_0_ROCMFPX_AGENT | Vulkan0 | 8.06 GiB | 1055.21 | 22.78 |\r | Q6_K | Vulkan0 | 7.08 GiB | 954.70 | 31.04 |\r \r ## Vulkan MMVQ Shape Probe\r \r The FP6 Vulkan `mul_mat_vecq` path was tested with larger `K_PER_ITER` values:\r \r | FP6 Vulkan shape | pp512 tok/s | tg128 tok/s | Decision |\r |---|---:|---:|---|\r | 8-wide default | 1055.21 | 22.78 | keep |\r | 16-wide | 1062.88 | 22.80 | reject; decode tie |\r | 32-wide | 1055.77 | 22.79 | reject; decode tie |\r \r The wider shapes pass Vulkan `MUL_MAT` correctness, but they do not improve decode.\r The source is restored to the 8-wide default.\r \r ## Vul","id":"fix_lessons:ROCmFPX\\docs\\ROCmFP6-DECODE-FOLLOWUP.md","metadata":{"extension":"md","geometry_map":[-0.030139774084091187,0.042964596301317215,0.037192899733781815,0.026196615770459175,0.03159676119685173,0.037155769765377045,0.03141755983233452,-0.02105511538684368,-0.03062475472688675,0.0025647440925240517],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\docs\\ROCmFP6-DECODE-FOLLOWUP.md","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.30000001192092896,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":4902},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"file_map","content":"ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-sycl\\template-instances\\fattn-vec-instance-q5_1-q5_0.cpp: // This file has been autogenerated by generate_cu_files.py, do not edit manually.\r \r #include \"../fattn-vec.hpp\"\r \r DECL_FATTN_VEC_CASE( 64, GGML_TYPE_Q5_1, GGML_TYPE_Q5_0);\r DECL_FATTN_VEC_CASE(128, GGML_TYPE_Q5_1, GGML_TYPE_Q5_0);\r DECL_FATTN_VEC_CASE(256, GGML_TYPE_Q5_1, GGML_TYPE_Q5_0);\r DECL_FATTN_VEC_CASE(512, GGML_TYPE_Q5_1, GGML_TYPE_Q5_0);\r ","id":"file_map:ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-sycl\\template-instances\\fattn-vec-instance-q5_1-q5_0.cpp","metadata":{"extension":"cpp","geometry_map":[-0.04860970750451088,0.03815688565373421,0.025237254798412323,0.0410990