roplet, copy the `ssh` command it gives you (e.g. `ssh user@129.x.x.x`). Clock is now running.  ## 2. Get the pipeline + your data onto the node From the workstation (Git Bas","id":"fix_lessons:RENTAL.md","metadata":{"extension":"md","geometry_map":[-0.035114504396915436,0.04279844090342522,0.04300634190440178,-0.03838333487510681,-0.02660764940083027,-0.037933871150016785,-0.015640761703252792,-0.023653892800211906,-0.01060294546186924,0.037355948239564896],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\RENTAL.md","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.30000001192092896,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":4072},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"file_map","content":"ROCmFPX\\examples\\model-conversion\\scripts\\embedding\\run-converted-model.sh: #!/usr/bin/env bash\r \r set -e\r \r # Parse command line arguments\r CONVERTED_MODEL=\"\"\r PROMPTS_FILE=\"\"\r EMBD_NORMALIZE=\"2\"\r \r while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\r     case $1 in\r         -p|--prompts-file)\r             PROMPTS_FILE=\"$2\"\r             shift 2\r             ;;\r         --embd-normalize)\r             EMBD_NORMALIZE=\"$2\"\r             shift 2\r             ;;\r         *)\r             if [ -z \"$CONVERT","id":"file_map:ROCmFPX\\examples\\model-conversion\\scripts\\embedding\\run-converted-model.sh","metadata":{"extension":"sh","geometry_map":[-0.031830016523599625,0.037527184933423996,0.03178473562002182,0.029669735580682755,0.028819628059864044,0.04764383286237717,0.03286442533135414,-0.027641132473945618,-0.013234366662800312,0.002832215279340744],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\examples\\model-conversion\\scripts\\embedding\\run-converted-model.sh","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.0,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":1448},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"fix_lessons","content":"ROCmFPX\\examples\\speculative-simple\\README.md: # llama.cpp/examples/speculative-simple\r \r Demonstration of basic greedy speculative decoding\r \r ```bash\r ./bin/llama-speculative-simple \\\r     -m  ../models/qwen2.5-32b-coder-instruct/ggml-model-q8_0.gguf \\\r     -md ../models/qwen2.5-1.5b-coder-instruct/ggml-model-q4_0.gguf \\\r     -f test.txt -c 0 -ngl 99 --color on \\\r     --sampling-seq k --top-k 1 -fa on --temp 0.0 \\\r     -ngld 99 --spec-draft-n-max 16 --spec-draft-n-draft-min 5 --draft-p-min 0.9\r ```\r ","id":"fix_lessons:ROCmFPX\\examples\\speculative-simple\\README.md","metadata":{"extension":"md","geometry_map":[-0.037597618997097015,0.038757991045713425,0.02470184676349163,0.033163584768772125,0.03511788323521614,0.041587863117456436,0.04078114777803421,-0.032100874930620193,-0.006384707055985928,0.005580123048275709],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\examples\\speculative-simple\\README.md","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.0,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":460},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"fix_lessons","content":"ROCmFPX\\docs\\development\\token_generation_performance_tips.md: # Token generation performance troubleshooting\r \r ## Verifying that the model is running on the GPU with CUDA\r Make sure you compiled llama with the correct env variables according to [this guide](/docs/build.md#cuda), so that llama accepts the `-ngl N` (or `--n-gpu-layers N`) flag. When running llama, you may configure `N` to be very large, and llama will offload the maximum possible number of layers to the GPU, even if it's less than the number you configured. For example:\r ```shell\r ./llama-cli -m \"path/to/model.gguf\" -ngl 200000 -p \"Please sir, may I have some \"\r ```\r \r When running llama, before it starts the inference work, it will output diagnostic information that shows whether cuBLAS is offloading work to the GPU. Look for these lines:\r ```shell\r llama_model_load_internal: [cublas] offloading 60 layers to GPU\r llama_model_load_internal: [cublas] offloading output layer to GPU\r llama_model_load_internal: [cublas] total VRAM used: 17223 MB\r ... rest of inference\r ```\r \r If you see these lines, then the GPU is being used.\r \r ## Verifying that the CPU is not oversaturated\r llama accepts a `-t N` (or `--threads N`) parameter. It's extremely important that this parameter is not ","id":"fix_lessons:ROCmFPX\\docs\\development\\token_generation_performance_tips.md","metadata":{"extension":"md","geometry_map":[-0.028965914621949196,0.04390221834182739,0.035627998411655426,0.025776395574212074,0.027772439643740654,0.042253416031599045,0.02655218355357647,-0.024455998092889786,-0.022055966779589653,0.00778143061324954],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\docs\\development\\token_generation_performance_tips.md","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.30000001192092896,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":2342},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"file_map","content":"ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-opencl\\kernels\\silu.cl: #pragma OPENCL EXTENSION cl_khr_fp16 : enable\r \r //------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r // silu\r //------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r kernel void kernel_silu(\r         global float * src0,\r         ulong offset0,\r         global float * dst,\r         ulong offsetd\r ) {\r     src0 = (global float*)((global char*)","id":"file_map:ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-opencl\\kernels\\silu.cl","metadata":{"extension":"cl","geometry_map":[-0.04966050758957863,0.03882823511958122,0.028458327054977417,0.04220249131321907,0.0327896922826767,0.03269937261939049,0.03581134229898453,-0.027798065915703773,-0.018480194732546806,0.018468478694558144],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-opencl\\kernels\\silu.cl","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.0,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":927},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"file_map","content":"ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-webgpu\\wgsl-sh