curity":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.30000001192092896,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":3456},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"fix_lessons","content":"ROCmFPX\\examples\\parallel\\README.md: # llama.cpp/example/parallel\r \r Simplified simulation of serving incoming requests in parallel\r \r ## Example\r \r Generate 128 client requests (`-ns 128`), simulating 8 concurrent clients (`-np 8`). The system prompt is shared (`-pps`), meaning that it is computed once at the start. The client requests consist of up to 10 junk questions (`--junk 10`) followed by the actual question.\r \r ```bash\r llama-parallel -m model.gguf -np 8 -ns 128 --top-k 1 -pps --junk 10 -c 16384\r ```\r \r > [!NOTE]\r > It's recommended to use base models with this example. Instruction tuned models might not be able to properly follow the custom chat template specified here, so the results might not be as expected.\r ","id":"fix_lessons:ROCmFPX\\examples\\parallel\\README.md","metadata":{"extension":"md","geometry_map":[-0.03636819124221802,0.04189407080411911,0.03126810863614082,0.03226384148001671,0.028950657695531845,0.04524275287985802,0.03300061449408531,-0.030274810269474983,-0.013397379778325558,0.007443475071340799],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\examples\\parallel\\README.md","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.0,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":694},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"file_map","content":"ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-vulkan\\vulkan-shaders\\flash_attn_mmq_v_funcs.glsl: // MMQ V-side helpers, asymmetric form. Mirrors flash_attn_mmq_funcs.glsl but\r // dispatches on FaTypeV and reads from the V bindings in flash_attn_dequant.glsl.\r \r int32_t get_v_qs(uint ib, uint iqs, uint a_offset) {\r     switch (FaTypeV) {\r         case FA_TYPE_Q4_0_ROCMFP4: {\r             const uint qbase = iqs & 0xFu;\r             uint vui = pack32(u8vec4(v_packed_rocmfp4.data[a_offset + ib].q","id":"file_map:ROCmFPX\\