-, 3-, 4-, 6-, and 8-bit GGUF model-weight\r formats to `llama.cpp`, with CPU reference paths and accelerated HIP/ROCm and\r Vulkan kernels.\r \r > **Status:** ROCmFPX is an experimental feature family on the canonical `main`\r > branch. APIs, tuning choices, and performance can change. Results depend on\r > hardware, drivers, model, prompt, and quantization recipe; use BF16/F16 sources\r > for quality comparisons.\r \r ## Disclosure\r \r **#AD #AMDAI**\r \r A huge thank you to AMD for providing the hardware that powers the ongoing\r development of ROCmFPX.\r \r The development system provided by AMD includes:\r \r - AMD Ryzen™ Threadripper™ 9980X\r - AMD Radeon™ AI PRO R9700 GPU\r - 128 GB ECC DDR5 Memory\r - 2 TB NVMe SSD\r \r This hardware enables me to continue developing, optimizing, benchmarking, and\r testing ROCmFPX for the community. AMD provided this hardware as part of a\r creator partnership. All development, benchmarks, code, testing, documentation,\r and opinions shared in this repository are my own.\r \r Thank you, AMD, for supporting the continued advancement of open AI development\r on Radeon hardware.\r \r **#AD #AMDAI**\r \r ## De","id":"fix_lessons:ROCmFPX\\README.md","metadata":{"extension":"md","geometry_map":[-0.04788661748170853,0.03552604839205742,0.028103001415729523,0.0337989404797554,0.024519626051187515,0.03175480663776398,0.03849029541015625,-0.028932901099324226,-0.012210499495267868,0.013842686079442501],"path":"C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\finetuneqwen3.827b\\ROCmFPX\\README.md","security":{"audit_needed":false,"risk_level":0.30000001192092896,"security_tier":"STANDARD"},"size":32570},"tags":[],"timestamp":1786891162},{"category":"file_map","content":"ROCmFPX\\ggml\\src\\ggml-hexagon\\htp\\hvx-reduce.h: #ifndef HVX_REDUCE_H\r #define HVX_REDUCE_H\r \r #include <math.h>\r #include <stdbool.h>\r #include <stdint.h>\r #include <assert.h>\r \r #include \"hex-utils.h\"\r #include \"hvx-base.h\"\r #include \"hvx-types.h\"\r \r static inline 